	(global_label "HTR_DRIVE"
		(shape output)
		(at 143.5100 267.9700 0)
		(fields_autoplaced yes)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.2700 1.2700)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e1e85c36-4333-2905-30df-6808d7635890")
		(property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}"
			(at 153.6700 267.9700 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.2700 1.2700)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		)
	)
	(text_box "WHAT THE GATE DOES BEFORE SOFTWARE WRITES THE DAC.\nThe 100k holds all three gates down whenever the DAC is not driving them, which covers an unpopulated or unpowered DAC and\nthe moment before the first I2C write. It does NOT cover the DAC powering up from its own EEPROM into something other than\nzero - and half scale is exactly the point of MAXIMUM pass-element dissipation, 0.8 W in each of three SOT-223s.  The fix\nis to program the MCP4725's EEPROM to zero once, at bring-up, with a Write-DAC-and-EEPROM command; the part then powers up\noff every time.  DATASHEET NEEDED to confirm the as-shipped EEPROM value - see the datasheet list in the notes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.7200 246.3800 0)
		(size 275.5900 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 245 210 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "38aa8b0f-35e5-2e88-96e2-4bd2a2e33c5f")
	)
	(text_box "WHY A DAC AND A LINEAR PASS FET, AND NOT PWM.\nPWM is the cheap way to drive a heater and it is the wrong way here.  Switching amperes of heater current a few hundred\ntimes a second puts that fundamental and its harmonics into the ground plane and into the supply, and this board's whole\njob is measuring picoseconds of phase.  A 12-bit DAC into a linear pass FET dissipates more and radiates nothing.  The\nloop itself is Python on the PYNQ: read a TMP1075, write the DAC, integrate."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.7200 215.9000 0)
		(size 275.5900 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 245 210 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "72b11ec3-43e0-c768-8376-a8ca0ec2935b")
	)
	(text_box "12-bit DAC straight onto the pass FET's gate.  The temperature loop runs in\nPython on the PYNQ: read a TMP1075, write the DAC, integrate.  Nothing switches,\nand it costs no header pins because it shares the I2C bus with the thermometers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.0200 218.4400 0)
		(size 121.9200 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f0466923-e264-e53d-1731-62a0fe21fd18")
	)
